  "semantics": [
    "Query reads the message DWORD at MSG+4 from identified CWnd::GetCurrentMessage, not a DC handle. It forwards this DWORD to the actual palette helper and preserves the entire32-bit return, including zero/high bits.",
    "Palette change compares CWnd object identity with this before calling IsChild. For a null notifying pointer, IsChild receives a null HWND; a zero IsChild result still reaches Query. Different CWnd objects holding equal HWNDs are not the self case.",
    "The child check uses receiver HWND at+0x1c and nullable notifying HWND at+0x1c. Its BOOL return uses a full zero test. APIs may change palette/DC/fullscreen state before the actual Query consumes it.",
    "Cursor reads the existing fullscreen BYTE. Any nonzero value calls SetCursor(NULL) and returns literalTRUE, including API failure or a callback changing fullscreen. Zero forwards the original three arguments and receiver to unmodified CFrameWnd::OnSetCursor, preserving its full return.",
    "Existing palette6700 and presentation6620 sources are unchanged. Whole128/224-byte contributions remain diagnostic-equal. Live palette/DC/owner reloads,dirty handling,StretchDIBits/GdiFlush,fullscreen Flip and fallback GetDC/GetClientRect/FillRect/ReleaseDC branches execute as original game code."
  ],
